{"annotationScore": 5.0, "comments": [{"commentType": "FUNCTION", "texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "id": "19889947", "source": "PubMed"}], "value": "Predominant protein in semen. It participates in the formation of a gel matrix entrapping the accessory gland secretions and ejaculated spermatozoa. Fragments of semenogelin and/or fragments of the related proteins may contribute to the activation of progressive sperm movements as the gel-forming proteins are fragmented by KLK3/PSA"}]}, {"commentType": "FUNCTION", "texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "id": "19889947", "source": "PubMed"}], "value": "Alpha-inhibin-92 and alpha-inhibin-31, derived from the proteolytic degradation of semenogelin, inhibit the secretion of pituitary follicle-stimulating hormone"}]}, {"commentType": "SUBUNIT", "texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "id": "15590901", "source": "PubMed"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "id": "17567961", "source": "PubMed"}], "value": "Occurs in disulfide-linked complexes which may also contain two less abundant 71- and 76-kDa semenogelin-related polypeptides. Interacts with EPPIN (via C-terminus); Cys-239 is a critical amino acid for both binding to EPPIN"}]}, {"commentType": "INTERACTION", "interactions": [{"interactantOne": {"intActId": "EBI-953955", "uniProtKBAccession": "P04279"}, "interactantTwo": {"geneName": "COLGALT2", "intActId": "EBI-10263496", "uniProtKBAccession": "Q8IYK4"}, "numberOfExperiments": 2, "organismDiffer": false}, {"interactantOne": {"intActId": "EBI-953955", "uniProtKBAccession": "P04279"}, "interactantTwo": {"geneName": "TET2", "intActId": "EBI-310727", "uniProtKBAccession": "Q6N021"}, "numberOfExperiments": 2, "organismDiffer": false}, {"interactantOne": {"intActId": "EBI-12272118", "uniProtKBAccession": "P04279-2"}, "interactantTwo": {"geneName": "EAF1", "intActId": "EBI-769261", "uniProtKBAccession": "Q96JC9"}, "numberOfExperiments": 3, "organismDiffer": false}, {"intera